{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"9bc3507996f8b99c","name":"card_event_home_defense","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Base/events/card_event_home_defense","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"HOME DEFENSE","text":"Costs 4 if your HQ is at 10 or less. Add TYPE 3 CHI-NU and AICHI D3A-2 to the support line.","flavorText":"A series of battles and engagements between the American and Japanese forces took place in and round the Japanese Home Islands during the final stages of WWII. There were two major island battles: The Battle of Iwo Jima and the Battle of Okinawa, and one naval battles: Operation Ten-Go. Including the aforementioned engagements, the American conducted air raids and naval bombardment on Japanese cities. However, the Japanese forces refused to surrender, and although the Americans were victorious they had to pay a steep price. Japan still had a homeland army of approximately two million soldiers and enough resources to halt an Allied invasion for a considerable time. However, it never came to use since Japan surrendered after the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":8,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_home_defense","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_home_defense_title","SourceString":"HOME DEFENSE","LocalizedString":"HOME DEFENSE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":8,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_home_defense_text","SourceString":"Costs 4 if your HQ is at 10 or less. Add TYPE 3 CHI-NU and AICHI D3A-2 to the support line.","LocalizedString":"Costs 4 if your HQ is at 10 or less. Add TYPE 3 CHI-NU and AICHI D3A-2 to the support line."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_home_defense_history","SourceString":"A series of battles and engagements between the American and Japanese forces took place in and round the Japanese Home Islands during the final stages of WWII. There were two major island battles: The Battle of Iwo Jima and the Battle of Okinawa, and one naval battles: Operation Ten-Go. Including the aforementioned engagements, the American conducted air raids and naval bombardment on Japanese cities. However, the Japanese forces refused to surrender, and although the Americans were victorious they had to pay a steep price. Japan still had a homeland army of approximately two million soldiers and enough resources to halt an Allied invasion for a considerable time. However, it never came to use since Japan surrendered after the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki.","LocalizedString":"A series of battles and engagements between the American and Japanese forces took place in and round the Japanese Home Islands during the final stages of WWII. There were two major island battles: The Battle of Iwo Jima and the Battle of Okinawa, and one naval battles: Operation Ten-Go. Including the aforementioned engagements, the American conducted air raids and naval bombardment on Japanese cities. However, the Japanese forces refused to surrender, and although the Americans were victorious they had to pay a steep price. Japan still had a homeland army of approximately two million soldiers and enough resources to halt an Allied invasion for a considerable time. However, it never came to use since Japan surrendered after the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","isInPermanentPool":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDealDamage","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnAfterOtherCardGainDefense","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnAfterOtherCardDefenseIsSet"],"spawnCardName":"card_unit_type_3_chi_nu;card_unit_aichi_d3a","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_2.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathNam